{"w": 595.3200073242188, "h": 809.0257568359375, "lines": [{"t": "154", "x": 0.8949472934591233, "y": 0.9742087522985531, "w": 0.03879595514451251, "h": 0.017428414981790374, "c": 1, "size": 12.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Speaker 1 (Tamara): Well, what about that one in Finland which showed that", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.12319506908974809, "w": 0.826435736384968, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "loneliness increased the risk of cancer by about 10%. And those findings have", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.15152541916388573, "w": 0.8260989419117193, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "been supported by other studies, too.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.17970752416545568, "w": 0.38852264412265963, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Speaker 2 (Dev): You're right about that one. I was actually thinking of the studies", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2080378742395933, "w": 0.826364891641889, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "on dementia. Some found no association between loneliness and dementia and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.23636822431373095, "w": 0.8261748103775348, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "others found the opposite.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.26469857438786853, "w": 0.2776578492130646, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Speaker 1 (Tamara): Not exactly reliable. Then there's been a lot of research on", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.2930660423122369, "w": 0.8262436046215379, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "cardiovascular disease and whether loneliness contributes to that.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.32139637352567824, "w": 0.6833052620009816, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Speaker 2 (Dev): Yes, I read that it was hard to reach a judgment. as the definition", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3497267990426009, "w": 0.8263867294570494, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "of loneliness varied quite a lot and the responses from participants were too", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.3780571491167385, "w": 0.8260989419117193, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "subjective. but there's no doubt that loneliness contributes to a weakened", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.40638753691226864, "w": 0.8260987368618117, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "immune system.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4347178869864063, "w": 0.17520876387406123, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Speaker 1 (Tamara): unquestionably the data on that is sound.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.4630482747819364, "w": 0.639967246353008, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Speaker 2 (Dev): what did you think about the evolutionary theory of loneliness?", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.49140337008956114, "w": 0.824842601127795, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Speaker 1 (Tamara): well I thought the idea that loneliness evolved because it", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5197337201636988, "w": 0.8261992113165404, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "motivated people to be with other people quite convincing. Survival often", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5480641079592289, "w": 0.8266594458341702, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "depended on group cooperation.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.5763944580333665, "w": 0.33974214256443414, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Speaker 1 (Tamara): But I don't think there's enough evidence to claim that there", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6047248458288966, "w": 0.8262458601705216, "h": 0.01882263537038409, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "must be a group of neurons in our brains which influence social behavior by", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6330551959030343, "w": 0.8259682225956181, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "making us feel bad when we're alone.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6612743433120499, "w": 0.39053833597693927, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Speaker 2 (Dev): There are a few studies which support the theory, but not", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.6896046933861876, "w": 0.8261871133719914, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "conclusively enough. More evidence is needed.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7179351189031102, "w": 0.4853109166622837, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Speaker 1 (Tamara): And anyway, this theory is not really useful when it comes to", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7462654689772478, "w": 0.8264573691502209, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "solving the problem of loneliness today. Hey,", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.7745958190513854, "w": 0.46616156210300413, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}, {"t": "Speaker 2 (Dev): true.", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8029261691255231, "w": 0.23452139762427127, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "Speaker 1 (Tamara): Should we look at the relationship between loneliness and", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8312565191996607, "w": 0.8262886130762581, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": true}, {"t": "mental health now?", "x": 0.10727675473252624, "y": 0.8596116899500704, "w": 0.21033271090433878, "h": 0.018822673091776602, "c": 1, "size": 13.0, "bold": false}], "source": "pdf text layer"}